                <invention-title lang="de">COMPUTERTOMOGRAFIESYSTEM FÜR FRACHT- UND TRANSPORTIERTE BEHÄLTER</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">SYSTÈME DE TOMOGRAPHIE PAR ORDINATEUR POUR MARCHANDISES ET CONTENEURS TRANSPORTÉS</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">COMPUTED TOMOGRAPHY SYSTEM FOR CARGO AND TRANSPORTED CONTAINERS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An imaging system includes an x-ray or gamma ray source (1) that emits an x-ray or gamma ray beam (3), a tunnel (20) having a plurality of detectors (10), and a translatable platform (34). The detectors (10) each receive a portion (3a-3g) of the beam (3). The translatable platform (34) supports cargo or a transported container (33) and moves through the tunnel (20) so that the cargo or transported container crosses the portions (3a-3g) of the beam (3) received by the detectors (10). The translatable platform (34) may move (S4, S6, S8, S10) through the tunnel (20). The imaging system may also include a computer (95, 96, 98). The computer (95, 96, 98) may receive information collected by the detectors (10) and may reconstruct (S21) a three-dimensional image of the cargo or transported container (33).</p>
            </abstract>
